{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1013 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "cabbd7ac9846a67856abfb357c6e664c21da7a9f1a8aed23ee71193fdb0843b6" :edb/db-before-t 1012 :edb/db-after-t 1013 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534325 50 #inst "2026-10-11T19:12:02.802Z" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186200200 1078 #edb/ref 17592186200202 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186203918 1038 #edb/ref 17592186419024 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186204249 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186204249 1071 "Suppose we have the sets $A$ and $B$, given by\n\n$A = {0.5, 2, \\sqrt{5}}, B = {-1, 0, 1}$.\n\nWhich of the following mapping diagrams represents the following relation?\n$R = {(x, y) ∈ A \\cdot B: x^{y} ∈ Z}$" 13194139534325 17592186045417 false] [17592186204249 1071 "Suppose we have the sets $A$ and $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={0.5,2,\\sqrt{5}},\\,B={-1,0,1}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following mapping diagrams represents the following relation? \n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in A\\times B\\,:\\,{x}^{y}\\in Z}\n$$" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186204249 1074 "The ordered pairs belonging to our relation correspond to the arrows on the mapping diagram. Each arrow starts at the first component of the pair and ends at its second component.\n\nWe're given the following sets:\n\n$$\nA={0.5,2,\\sqrt{5}},\\,B={-1,0,1}.\n$$\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in A\\times B$ with ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$\n\n- If $x=0.5,$ then the values $y=-1,0$ satisfy ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(0.5,-1)$ and $(0.5,0),$ and we should add the arrows $0.5\\to -1$ and $0.5\\to 0$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=2,$ then the values $y=0,1$ satisfy ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(2,0)$ and $(2,1),$ and we should add the arrows $2\\to 0$ and $2\\to 1$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=\\sqrt{5},$ then the value $y=0$ satisfies ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(\\sqrt{5},0),$ and we should add the arrow $\\sqrt{5}\\to 0$ to the mapping diagram.\n\nTherefore, we have the following plot:\n\n![](images/d6/d66cabe448b2b33804721dd3cfa884de858a5e4fa6056991f612465070d54da5.png)" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419018 1080 "images/90/90f18f9bc042dda952e423a56268bd6b917db2f94f9a7b42ee8087290b169fa4.png" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419018 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419018 1083 #uuid "45d65c90-dfbc-57d3-96ca-a717e1f395a7" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419019 1080 "images/cd/cd9e524895740aa64ee6143d3d600d6be38b7e6e71b00d402ee249c11c3da36e.png" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419019 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419019 1083 #uuid "4b79f667-cd57-53d0-854e-fda5aee2821d" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419020 1080 "images/7b/7bac8457b66917fc1aa9866c04fddef3685196f48d68cd9ce40642b144cb41aa.png" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419020 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419020 1083 #uuid "d174cbc8-3270-5fcf-b235-c7e8a0ccc0cc" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419021 1080 "images/3a/3a95797dc283876f7b5c4d71c1f954481cb5d21caa7a1c5acbdaec952991c84f.png" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419021 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419021 1083 #uuid "f24e9d57-53f5-569d-babd-8bd097337ac0" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419022 1080 "images/cc/cc35ab376bbc7156418f199895c2ff636e46b0955365ac6636156eb901075aa3.png" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419022 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419022 1083 #uuid "f7d312b2-66ec-592d-821c-8f851491b42f" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419018 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419019 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419020 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419021 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419022 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1077 "selection" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419019 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419023 1079 #uuid "b3d1d66b-023d-5750-9175-e0bf093e91da" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419024 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419023 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419024 1069 "q-213260" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419024 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419024 1071 "Suppose we have the set $A={1,2,3,4}.$ Which of the following mapping diagrams represents the following relation? \n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in A\\times A\\,:\\,x<y}\n$$" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419024 1072 #uuid "c266a8db-0d0c-5c54-9052-48c9757f64e6" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true] [17592186419024 1074 "The ordered pairs belonging to our relation correspond to the arrows on the mapping diagram. Each arrow starts at the first component of the pair and ends at its second component.\n\nWe're given the following set:\n\n$$\nA={1,2,3,4}.\n$$\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in A\\times A$ such that $x<y.$\n\n- If $x=1,$ then the values $y=2,3,4$ satisfy $x<y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(1,2),\\,(1,3),$ and $(1,4),$ and we should add the arrows $1\\to 2,\\,1\\to 3,$ and $1\\to 4$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=2,$ then the values $y=3,4$ satisfy $x<y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(2,3)$ and $(2,4),$ and we should add the arrows $2\\to 3$ and $2\\to 4$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=3,$ then the value $y=4$ satisfies $x<y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(3,4),$ and we should add the arrow $3\\to 4$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=4$ there are no values $y\\in A$ such that $x<y.$ Therefore we do not add arrows starting from $4$ to the mapping diagram.\n\nTherefore, we have the following plot:\n\n![](images/cd/cd9e524895740aa64ee6143d3d600d6be38b7e6e71b00d402ee249c11c3da36e.png)" 13194139534325 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-45d65c90-dfbc-57d3-96ca-a717e1f395a7" 17592186419018 "answer-4b79f667-cd57-53d0-854e-fda5aee2821d" 17592186419019 "answer-d174cbc8-3270-5fcf-b235-c7e8a0ccc0cc" 17592186419020 "answer-f24e9d57-53f5-569d-babd-8bd097337ac0" 17592186419021 "answer-f7d312b2-66ec-592d-821c-8f851491b42f" 17592186419022 "answer-field-b3d1d66b-023d-5750-9175-e0bf093e91da" 17592186419023 "question-c266a8db-0d0c-5c54-9052-48c9757f64e6" 17592186419024}}
